# Branch + PR Workflow

- Delivery unit is a short-lived branch + PR — not long-lived local-only edits on a shared branch.
- One focused change per PR (one page, feature, or bugfix).
- Branch from the latest base (`main` unless already on an agreed feature branch). Name like `feat/<area>-smoke` or `fix/<area>-<short-desc>`.
- For **Playwright / QA test-case** work: when implementation + targeted test pass, **commit and push** the feature branch immediately (see `test-case-branch-push` rule). Do not leave finished smokes stashed or local-only.
- For other non-test changes: when implementation work is finished, offer to commit, push, and open the PR (do not leave finished work unshipped without asking).
- Only open a PR after the user agrees, unless they already asked to ship/push/open a PR for that change.
- PR body: short summary + test plan checklist. Never force-push `main`/`master`.
